# #5851 D5 (a5e2e2ef, #5851 comment 6667620149): a write with no routing generation goes
# unstamped in dispatch whatever the fence returns (C4), even while the writer is a deferred
# sibling whose fence answers PreArm. Attributed to that sibling it is invisible to the owner.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestDeferredSiblingStampsUnrouted
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
PERTURBS: UnroutedAlloc
SUMMARY: while L is deferred, an unrouted write of one of L's keys by another leaf is stamped PreArm as its deferred fence answers, so it raises neither the shared watermark nor staleHigh, and L free-advances past it unapplied
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithSplitBirth = TRUE, WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1, WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ lastU' = next
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, acked, floor, leafVars, epochVars, handVars, envVars>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the deferred fence's PreArm is honoured for an unrouted write.
    /\ lastU' = IF ~moved /\ (pend \/ hoOpen) /\ ~eagerG /\ ~repair THEN lastU ELSE next
    /\ UNCHANGED <<durable, acked, floor, leafVars, epochVars, handVars, envVars>>
--- END
